<% title "Payout runs (Fuime)" %>

<%# FUIME: every weekly payout run, newest first.

    The second half of the manual-approval control. admin/operator_vetting decides
    who may sell; this decides what Fuime actually pays them, and nothing goes out
    without a human opening a run and reading it.

    See Fuime::PayoutBatchService for the lifecycle and Fuime::PayoutPolicy for the
    four dials each run is generated under. %>

<% unless @merchant_of_record %>
  <%# Not an error state. The flag is off on every environment that exists today
      and cannot be switched on without a counsel-memo reference at boot, so the
      honest thing is to say so here rather than let somebody click Generate and
      read a raised exception as a bug. %>
  <div class="card bg-warning mb2">
    <strong>Merchant of record is off.</strong>
    Fuime is not the seller of record, so it has no money of its own to pay out and
    runs cannot be generated. Operators are paid on the Connect path instead — money
    sits in the family's own Stripe account and a guardian approves each payout —
    until <code>FEATURE_MERCHANT_OF_RECORD</code> is enabled, which requires
    <code>FUIME_MOR_COUNSEL_MEMO</code> to cite a real memo at boot.
  </div>
<% end %>

<div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb2 flex-wrap">
  <% %w[draft approved paid cancelled].each do |state| %>
    <span class="badge <%= state == "draft" ? "bg-warning" : "bg-muted" %>">
      <%= state.humanize %>: <%= @counts[state] || 0 %>
    </span>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%= form_with url: payout_batch_generate_admin_index_path, method: :post, local: true, class: "card mb2" do |form| %>
  <p class="muted mt0">
    Runs are generated automatically each Wednesday for the Friday payout
    (<code>Fuime::GeneratePayoutBatchJob</code>). Generate one by hand only to
    replace a run that was cancelled, or to catch up a missed week — and set the
    period end to the week it settles, not to today.
  </p>
  <div class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
    <%= form.label :period_end, "Period ends" %>
    <%= form.date_field :period_end, value: Date.current %>
    <%= form.submit "Generate run", disabled: !@merchant_of_record %>
  </div>
<% end %>

<div class="flex items-center mb2 flex-col sm:flex-row">
  <div class="flex-grow">
    <%= page_entries_info @batches, entry_name: "runs" %>
  </div>
  <%= paginate @batches %>
</div>

<table class="min-w-0">
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th class="w-24">ID</th>
      <th>Pays on</th>
      <th>Period</th>
      <th>Operators</th>
      <th>Total</th>
      <th>Held as reserve</th>
      <th>State</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <% @batches.each do |batch| %>
      <tr class="<%= "admin-bg-pending" if batch.draft? %>">
        <td><%= link_to batch.id, payout_batch_admin_index_path(id: batch.id) %></td>
        <td><%= batch.payout_on.strftime("%a %-d %b %Y") %></td>
        <td class="muted">
          <%= batch.period_start.strftime("%-d %b") %> – <%= batch.period_end.strftime("%-d %b") %>
        </td>
        <td><%= batch.operator_count %></td>
        <td><%= render_money batch.total_cents %></td>
        <td class="muted"><%= render_money batch.reserve_held_cents %></td>
        <td>
          <%= batch.aasm_state.humanize %>
          <% if batch.approved_by %>
            <div class="muted">by <%= batch.approved_by.name %></div>
          <% end %>
        </td>
      </tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>

<%= paginate @batches %>
